---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import ResetStorage from '../components/ResetStorage.astro'
import { withBase } from '../lib/url'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Your data"
  description="What this site stores in your browser, and how to clear it."
>
  <article class="max-w-[720px] py-14 sm:py-20">
    <p class="eyebrow">Your data</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-[2rem] leading-[1.15] sm:text-[2.45rem]">What this site keeps</h1>

    <div class="prose-block mt-6 text-[0.98rem]">
      <p>
        This site has no accounts, no server-side storage and no analytics. The only thing it keeps
        is what you produce as you work through the weeks: which readings you have ticked, and the
        notes you write on each week. Both live in this browser, on this device, and are never sent
        anywhere.
      </p>
      <p>
        That also means they do not follow you. Clearing your browser data, using private browsing,
        or opening the site in another browser starts you from scratch. Nothing on the site is gated
        on your progress, so there is nothing to lose access to.
      </p>
      <p>
        More on how the group runs is on the <a href={withBase('/about')}>about page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ResetStorage />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
